criticalIssues.recommendation:
Clamp the actual sleep to the time remaining until the deadline. Replace the body of sleepWithDeadline with:

  private void sleepWithDeadline(long durationMs, Instant deadline, AtomicInteger attempts) {
    checkDeadline(deadline, attempts);
    if (durationMs <= 0) { checkDeadline(deadline, attempts); return; }
    long remainingMs = Math.max(0L, java.time.Duration.between(Instant.now(), deadline).toMillis());
    long actualSleepMs = Math.min(durationMs, remainingMs);
    if (actualSleepMs > 0) {
      try { Thread.sleep(actualSleepMs); }
      catch (InterruptedException ie) {
        Thread.currentThread().interrupt();
        throw new TelegramSendException(null, "interrupted", attempts.get());
      }
    }
    checkDeadline(deadline, attempts);
  }

The post-sleep checkDeadline will then fire deterministically right at the budget boundary, giving wall-clock parity with the prior Reactor .timeout(overallTimeout) behavior. After the fix, the 429LargeRetryAfter test elapsed will land around the SHORT_OVERALL_TIMEOUT (3s) ± jitter.
